=== docs/concepts/outbox.md <-> website/src/pages/learn/outbox.mdx: 33 only-in-docs, 33 only-in-website
  D: After the commit, the rows in events are the canonical record of what happened.
  D: And this is the table they land in - events has its DDL on every dialect, column by column.
  D: Assert on action_name or action_id rather than on position, or use a running clock.
  D: Every action's commit is one database transaction that touches as many domain tables as the action needs plus the outbox.
  D: How rows get there Every row arrives the same way, and no other way exists:
  D: In-process fan-out flips delivered from false to true, producing UPDATE rows;
  D: It is also what makes the generated schema module the single source of truth for the table's shape.
